# Code ownership for review routing (roadmap §5.5 governance).
#
# GitHub requests a review from the owner of every changed path. The security-
# critical surfaces are listed explicitly so a change to a guard, a bound, the
# sandbox, or the supply-chain tooling always reaches a reviewer. Later lines win,
# so the specific rules below override the catch-all.

# Default owner for everything not matched more specifically.
*                                   @chiaraberti13

# --- Security-critical core: SSRF guard, IP pinning, execution bounds and
#     redaction, editable policy, HTTP/decompression limits, retention. ---
/src/olympus/core/addresses.py      @chiaraberti13
/src/olympus/core/pinning.py        @chiaraberti13
/src/olympus/core/execution.py      @chiaraberti13
/src/olympus/core/policy.py         @chiaraberti13
/src/olympus/core/http.py           @chiaraberti13
/src/olympus/core/decompression.py  @chiaraberti13
/src/olympus/core/retention.py      @chiaraberti13

# --- AEGIS execution plane: sandbox isolation, scope gate, API identity. ---
